  "_comment": "Labels for keyword_cases.json (the correct answer, not the current output). class: exact_ref = the whole question is one ref token (ev:, file:, sym:, mem:, task:, commit:). symbol_definition = where or what is the definition of a named code thing. callers = who calls, uses or references a named function. timeline = about the PAST conversation, decisions, rules, or what the user or we said or chose; a question about why CODE behaves some way is NOT timeline (it is search). implementation = which commit or change implemented something. task = has a task ref (#123, ZC-42) and no stronger class. search = everything else. intent: edit = asks to change code (English edit verb first, or a Turkish edit verb at the end of the sentence; an edit verb in the middle of a sentence does not count); locate = asks which file or where to change, or where the code that does Y is (hangi dosyada, nerede, where is the); where X is defined is general, not locate; trace = a flow or path from A to B, or a call chain; memory = decisions, rules, history (timeline-like, commit history); a task ref (task class) also reads its history, so task-class questions without an edit verb are memory; explain = how or why code works; general = anything else (chat, 'devam et', generic requests). a call chain or flow question ('trace the call chain from A to B', 'cagri zincirini cikar') is class search, intent trace; set: every 3rd case (index % 3 == 2) is holdout, the rest dev. Holdout is for the gate; do not tune rules to it."
